{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>Let him forsake, etc.</b> Its meaning: they sought [it from] HaShem." "<b>His way.</b> That he is accustomed to walk in. And let the wicked man forsake his thoughts. Behold, the essence is thought and deed." "<b>For He multiplies pardon.</b> Of sins."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 55, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:59:39.317965400Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}